  "notes": "{慌|あわ}てる means to panic, become flustered, or act hastily due to surprise or urgency.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- No transitive pair\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{慌|あわ}てている describes being in a state of panic or fluster.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {慌|あわ}てないで: don't panic\n- {慌|あわ}てて + verb: do something hastily\n- {慌|あわ}て{者|もの}: hasty/careless person\n- {大慌|おおあわ}て: great panic\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {焦|あせ}る: to feel anxious, be impatient\n- {急|いそ}ぐ: to hurry (neutral)\n- パニックになる: to panic (loanword)\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\n{慌|あわ}てて is commonly used as an adverb meaning \"in a hurry\": {慌|あわ}てて{家|いえ}を{出|で}た (I left home in a hurry).",
